@api = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Log in as Alice (normal user)
# @name loginAlice
POST {{api}}/api/User/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice.nielsen@watchworld.dk",
  "password": "$2a$12$eImiTXuWVxfM37uY4JANjO5E/Qd/./v7YdZ2Y2q8.1M22.GfK1234"
}

### 2. Log in as Charlie (admin)
# @name loginCharlie
POST {{api}}/api/User/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@watchworld.dk",
  "password": "LeAdminos123!"
}

### 3. Wrong password, should give 401
POST {{api}}/api/User/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice.nielsen@watchworld.dk",
  "password": "Wrong123!"
}

### 4. Public endpoint, no token -> 200
GET {{api}}/api/Watches

### 5. Locked endpoint, no token -> 401
GET {{api}}/api/Borrow

### 6. Locked endpoint, Alice's token -> 200
GET {{api}}/api/Borrow
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAlice.response.body.$.token}}

### 7. Tampered token (one extra letter at the end) -> 401
GET {{api}}/api/Borrow
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAlice.response.body.$.token}}x

### 8. Admin-only endpoint, Alice's token -> 403
DELETE {{api}}/api/Watches/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAlice.response.body.$.token}}